    "body": "Added a \"Related\" note to the body after the claim; edits don't notify, so here it is.\n\nM13.11 already reads a plane as the union of touching bodies when the source is a selection across several models. `Material.bodies` is filled only in `material_of`'s `SrcRef::Selection` arm (`crates/app/src/operation/material.rs`), and `verify::verify_bodies` and `machining2d::contour_on_bodies` read it.\n\n`sample_ap214` arrives as one `SrcRef::Entity` holding three solids, so `bodies` stays empty and `material::section()` slices the plain facets. Filling `bodies` per solid for one model is a second route to the same union, beside welding in `slice()`.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
